THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The terms above cover the code and the original content written for Intonare. They do not cover third-party material included in this repository, which stays under its own licence. Those licences are listed in the app's Credits screen and summarised here:

- Performance MIDI sequences adapted from recordings by Bernd Krüger (piano-midi.de), CC BY-SA 3.0 Germany. The adapted files are published under the same licence in credits/midi-sources/, together with a description of what was changed.
- Bassoon and contrabassoon body diagrams by Bret Pimentel (fingering.bretpimentel.com), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, used with the author's written permission.
- Sheet music arrangements by Crazystride and OpenScore Lieder, CC BY 4.0; by Ivan Di Sipio, CC0 1.0; and from the Mutopia Project, public domain.
- Online quiz questions from the Open Trivia Database (opentdb.com), CC BY-SA 4.0, fetched at runtime rather than stored here.
- Instrument samples follow the naming conventions of the gleitz MIDI-js soundfonts and carry their original licences.

Where a third-party licence grants you rights that this file does not, that licence governs that material. Nothing here is intended to restrict it.
